// The Java binding's classes, compiled once and shared by the whole JVM
// family: kotlin/, scala/, clojure/ and groovy/ all layer over THESE classes
// rather than binding the engine a second time.
//
// Uses aeb's `java.javac` builder. `source_layout("maven idiomatic")` is
// REQUIRED, not decorative: without it javac only globs *.java at the module
// root (depth 1) and reports "no Java source files found" — a green no-op, not
// an error, which is an easy thing to miss. The important part is what it
// publishes: the standard
// `jvm_classpath_deps_including_transitive` artifact, which every JVM SDK
// builder reads through `bldr._build_dep_classpath(...)`. The hand-rolled
// javac shell-out this replaced published a bespoke `classes_dir` instead,
// which those builders cannot see — so migrating this node is what unblocks
// the kotlin/scala/groovy/clojure migrations.
//
// JDK 22+ is required: the binding is FFM/Panama (java.lang.foreign), final
// in 22. `release` is deliberately NOT pinned below that.

import bldr
import java
import java (source_layout)

aeb(cap) {
    bldr.build() {
        java.javac() {
            source_layout("maven idiomatic")   // sources live in src/main/java
        }
    }
}
